new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e714c29
--- /dev/null
+++ b/cloudflare/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+# Normativity Workers candidate — not deployment-ready
+
+Prepared against WebsiteBuilding2 `4ee214324976cf579a77bde4788551cfe32f94fb`.
+Everything in this directory is a compatibility-test candidate. Existing
+application files, Prisma models, Vercel configuration and lockfile are unchanged.
+Do not deploy this harness or use production credentials with it.
+
+## Smallest currently identified runtime adaptations
+
+- Prebundle as Node with esbuild, then tell Wrangler not to rebundle. This keeps
+  `iconv-lite`'s real stream implementation that browser mappings removed in the
+  first probe. An assertion stops the build if that implementation is missing.
+- Generate Prisma's JavaScript engine for `workerd`, using the matching 6.19.0
+  PostgreSQL driver adapter. A request-scoped facade preserves existing service
+  calls, creates connections lazily, and disconnects after the response.
+  Database models and migrations are not changed.
+- Replace two dynamic `new Function(... import ...)` JOSE loaders with normal
+  dynamic imports **in the bundle only**. Verification/signing logic is retained.
+- Exclude only the standalone Node listener/interval bootstrap from the bundle.
+  The Workers HTTP entry calls the existing Express app and existing public-config
+  and audit endpoint handlers. Production auth is enforced during the probe.
+
+## Verification boundary
+
+`node --test request-database.test.mjs transforms.test.mjs auth-negative.test.mjs`
+uses only Node built-ins. It verifies isolation, cleanup, exact source-preserving
+transformations and rejection of forged development headers. It does not prove
+database compatibility, valid JWT handling or Workers runtime success.
+
+The new dependencies have not been installed and no new lockfile has been
+resolved. Before installation/push, obtain the user's approval for the separately
+prepared free, isolated cloud test. Use only loopback synthetic database addresses.
+Never run the repository root postinstall, database migrations or remote tests.
+
+## Blockers to preserving every feature
+
+`server/src/services/tsa.ts` runs the OpenSSL executable to create RFC 3161
+timestamp requests and, when configured, verify timestamp responses against a CA.
+Workers cannot run that executable. This candidate deliberately leaves the
+feature unchanged and marks it **unresolved**, rather than skipping verification.
+
+This backend harness does not yet implement the frontend asset deployment or
+scheduled audit trigger. Scheduled execution must preserve the existing audit
+and timestamp behavior before a migration is approved. Full database operations,
+valid JWTs, signed proofs, Storage uploads, AI-provider behavior, frontend
+interactions and request/CPU limits also need isolated tests. Keep Vercel serving
+the complete application until those gates pass; a successful startup is
+insufficient.
